n outriders  known as the trickster each character we  pick  can harness three skills at once i'm  gonna stick to the first three you'll  encounter in the demo  for each class the first trickster  ability is temporal blade  which paralyzes and slices an enemy  right in front of your eyes  and more likely than not they'll explode  in a bony burst  oh it's satisfying the second ability is  the most awe-inspiring thing of beauty  the slow trap it's like a destiny titan  bubble  yet it's not a shield bullets can  permeate this  but once those bullets are inside they  slow down  and so do the enemies too slow motion  this allows us the trickster to get  heavy damage on foes  and teaming it with the first ability we  get this and if all that wasn't enough  the third ability  lets the trickster utilize something  called hunt the prey  it's basically a teleporter which lets  us land right behind the enemy  they do react pretty quickly but if you  have a shotgun this  can be ultra satisfying here's all three  powers in a single play  i've got a feeling i like this a little  too much and remember that's only the  first three abilities each class  has five more so the trickster  manipulates time and space to get up  close and personal with enemies but if  that's not your bag then try the  technomancer  a long range class with gadgets like  those found in borderlands  have a look-see the technomancer's first  ability is a grenade effectively  a mine which can be thrown pretty far  distances  it then waits to be triggered and pops  up to cause maximum damage  this is to keep enemies away from the  technomancer  range is key to this class the second  ability is the cryo turret  it's like a thrown down extra companion  which gains aggro  it deals freeze damage and can be used  to flank enemies or trap them  if you're playing solo this is a great  thing to have with you  but by far the best thing of the first  three abilities is the pain  launcher that's legit its name a missile  launcher that decimates everything it  hits  even working across chasms and behind  cover  really fun to use  let's go back to close up and in your  face action with the devastator  the devastator utilizes the ground  beneath our feet  to get the edge in battle these guys are  like the tank class of the group  and they're happy to take damage as long  as they're dealing damage  what makes this class feel great is the  third ability unlocked  the gravity leap we take to the skies  then select a target  to crush them with rocks and rubble  there's a certain satisfaction to using  your butt  as a weapon the devastator also has a  seismic interrupt which is a punch to  the ground  causing her like a micro earthquake of  damage and interrupts enemies  and finally look at this additional  armor is added which absorbs  65 percent of all attacks it's a thing  of beauty  and keep in mind there's another five  abilities to unlock after this point  like a spike that impales falls there's  some impressive mechanical depth here  and finally we have the pyromancer the  medium range jack of all trades  master of none class but this guy has  little fire  at their fingertips firstly you'll  unlock heatwave a wall of fire flies  towards and ignites enemies  putting them in a fit of panic we then  have the feed the flames ability which  is like a whip of fire  kinda like scorpions get over here in  moral combat  but not bringing them too close because  the pyromancer is a medium-range unit  it deals damage and inflicts ash 2. and  now we're talking  ability 3 is the thermal bomb take a  look at this  the ability burns an enemy and if their  health is low enough to eliminate them  they'll literally explode it's another  ability which does not get old it's a  thing of beauty  especially when there are other enemies  to take damage from that explosion  so which of these classes is for you i'm  a trickster main right now  get in hit and run get away and remember  those are only 12 unlockable  skills there's another 20 to find in  your own time there is far more to each  class but i wanted to show you  the wow factor things over the subtle  changes and boosts in stats  but if you'd like to know everything  about everything you should totally  check out the outriders  channel as it's packed with everything  you want to know about everything  for me i just want to feel like an evil  superhero  there's way more depth to outriders  which can be seen in the class skill  tree offering a plethora of ways to make  your character the exact way you want  them to be  points acquired in this demo and the  full game can be spent here  which should mean having three of the  same class in one group  will still see three totally different  builds in skills and abilities  this screen looks pretty daunting to me  but it's mainly stat boosts  and if we're unhappy with what we've  picked the tree can be reset  one of the things i admire most about  outriders is its insistence  for us to fight and not sit back that's  because we are rewarded with health and  buffs to play in aggressive ways  and although you can sit back the ai on  the bosses in particular will flush you  out  in this boss fight the minions will  flank around the outskirts while the  boss  who is also altered throws out a fire  tornado which hunts you down slowly  adding an element of spatial awareness  and planning where the heck do you run  to next to stay in charge of the fight  another boss will actually throw down an  electrified shrapnel to wherever you're  stood  and backs it up with a watchlight of  electricity which we must run away from  regardless of position  thanks to those small things the game  feels consistently fast paced  instinctive and aggressive and it's a  welcome adrenaline rush  just in case you weren't aware outriders  is a team-based affair  i personally like playing these games  alone but i know i'm weird like that  this is ideally a three-person adventure  i played randoms a few times but the  most fun i had was with a friend  when we attempted a no-guns playthrough  it was tough but only using abilities  is extremely fun  you'll notice my characters keep  changing appearance it's because our  characters can be altered whenever we  see fit  once we've made our initial decision  this isn't anything world shattering but  there's enough facial type  scars and variants of hair to keep most  of us happy  i'm keen not to go overly detailed on  things right now i definitely think you  should play the demo and see for  yourself if outriders is a game for you  and should you want more coverage just  let me know oh in fact there is another  piece of info you should know about this  demo and it's that your progress during  this time will be taken forward  into the full game all your efforts are  recorded and rewarded  should you choose to you could find as  many journal entries as possible  or maybe mind for iron and gather scrap  which in turn will make your experience  in the full game  more plentiful whilst you're at it look  out for those exotic weapons  which have a tiny chance of dropping in  the demo i've seen some impressive stuff  on twitter and youtube  but i can't find any myself maybe you  could be the one  to find the next ultra rare loot drop i  think this is a good time to end this  i'm going back to my tricks to maine  i'll see you on the battlefield  i'm adam from playstation grenade thanks  again to square enix for sponsoring this  video  i'll see you all next time  [Music]  you
 

